{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EVo3ZYhSRN1sXx3YqWgj5v","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t//go:build bdd\n2\t\n3\t// Package steps holds the step definitions for the `mcp` suite\n4\t// (tests/mcp), the suite that owns the mcp-service scenarios of\n5\t// docs/scenarios.yaml.\n6\t//\n7\t// Every definition is registered in Register and implemented against\n8\t// *State, the single state type this suite shares: Given prepares, When\n9\t// acts, Then asserts and returns an error naming what it expected and\n10\t// what it got. New definitions belong in Register below — not in a\n11\t// second registry.\n12\tpackage steps\n13\t\n14\timport (\n15\t\t\"bytes\"\n16\t\t\"encoding/json\"\n17\t\t\"fmt\"\n18\t\t\"io\"\n19\t\t\"net\"\n20\t\t\"net/http\"\n21\t\t\"net/url\"\n22\t\t\"os\"\n23\t\t\"regexp\"\n24\t\t\"strconv\"\n25\t\t\"strings\"\n26\t\t\"time\"\n27\t)\n28\t\n29\tconst (\n30\t\tdefaultPort    = 8080\n31\t\treadyTimeout   = 10 * time.Second\n32\t\treadyInterval  = 100 * time.Millisecond\n33\t\trequestTimeout = 10 * time.Second\n34\t\tmaxBodyBytes   = 1 << 20\n35\t)\n36\t\n37\t// State is the per-scenario state every step definition in this suite\n38\t// reads and writes. One value exists per scenario run.\n39\ttype State struct {\n40\t\t// BaseURL is the root this suite posts to, e.g. http://127.0.0.1:8080.\n41\t\t// Empty until a Given step has located the server.\n42\t\tBaseURL string\n43\t\t// Port is the port the server was found accepting connections on.\n44\t\tPort int\n45\t\t// Client is reused by every request-issuing step.\n46\t\tClient *http.Client\n47\t\n48\t\t// LastMethod is the JSON-RPC method of the most recent request.\n49\t\tLastMethod string\n50\t\t// LastEndpoint is the full URL of the most recent request.\n51\t\tLastEndpoint string\n52\t\t// StatusCode is the HTTP status of the most recent response, or 0\n53\t\t// when no request has been issued yet.\n54\t\tStatusCode int\n55\t\t// Body is the body of the 